WEBVTT

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.450
<i>As the weekend was approaching,</i>

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>Tonegawa was suddenly summoned 
by President Hyoudou.</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.970
Excuse me.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.710
Bored.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.670
<i>It's déjà vu!</i>

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.680
This is dull. I'm fed up.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.060
<i>Tonegawa has seen this!</i>

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.570
<i>Six months ago, he saw the 
president in this state!</i>

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.190
<i>An omen of extreme tyranny and madness!</i>

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:48.530
<i>The door to carnage opens anew!</i>

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.440
<i>The bottomless bog!</i>

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.700
<i>Death descends once more 
at the Gate of Hell!</i>

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.550
Television, movies, music, it's all a farce.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.750
This pablum about love, romance,

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.460
how we're not alone in the world... 
Longing to see someone,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:11.210
but then not wanting to see them, 
but ultimately they do?

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:17.220
"My bangs are too short!" "My jeans are 
too tight!" and all their complaints...

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.720
<b>Psst...</b>

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.720
None of them understand 
what it means to be human.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.730
It's a sham. It's a mockery.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.610
I want to see something authentic, 
and I want a front row seat.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.230
The ugliest side of humanity, 
the most extreme of extremes...

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.930
Our true nature: destruction, despair...

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.240
and death.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.220
Now that is true entertainment. Sincere joy.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.120
Don't you agree, Tonegawa, my boy?

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.750
Yes, sir, I do.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.550
I can arrange for another 
game of Restricted—

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:56.760
Not enough!

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.530
I need a more intense diversion,

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.770
one that causes my blood to 
pump and my flesh to quiver...

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.510
Something far, far, far more extreme!

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.870
Where the scumbags at the ends 
of their ropes squirm and struggle,

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.970
demonstrating the truth of human nature!

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.780
A game of death, where it's kill or be killed!

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.970
<i>I see...</i>

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.800
<i>The reason they're all quiet when 
they'd usually pipe up is because</i>

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.270
<i>the president is being more 
unreasonable than usual!</i>

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:31.250
I want to see something even more 
genuine. Don't you see, Tonegawa?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.420
Don't look at me like that!

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.170
I understand, sir.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:43.770
<i>Tonegawa is once again faced with
a trial on the verge of his weekend!</i>

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.440
<i>Yet again, it all falls apart! 
My weekend golf plans are up in smoke!</i>

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.170
I can begin the planning process 
for another death game—

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.440
I've already come up with it.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.630
My own idea for a game of death!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:17.010
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:17.010
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.460
I know this is sudden,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.800
<i>Agenda 24
<b></b></i>\h\h\h\h\h\hEnd of the Line

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.260
but in three days, at 8:00 PM,

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.720
at Starside Hotel, 
President Hyoudou's personally devised

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.270
diabolical event with debtors 
as participants will be held.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.810
The Starside Hotel? 
The one our company owns?

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:58.520
<b>Psst...</b>

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.520
But isn't it still under construction?

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.530
Right. It's not opening until 
the year after next.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.400
And the president came up 
with this game himself?

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.160
Human Derby.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.820
Human... Derby?

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:14.410
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.410
<i>The name alone creates a deep impact!</i>

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.670
The first game is going to be set up 
and overseen by another team,

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.170
but Team Tonegawa may be responsible 
for running it again at a future date.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:28.110
Thus, we'll be present to observe...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.550
S-Sir!

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.810
What kind of game is this Human Derby?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.810
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.640
Well...

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.490
I can't say!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.490
It's too diabolical to put into words.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:50.280
If I were to explain, you people would 
be disgusted. Maybe even freak out!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.280
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.600
The president's ideas are truly abnormal...

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.860
A step or two beyond what any 
sane person would ever consider!

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.440
It's a genuinely destructive diversion, 
this Human Derby!

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.300
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.300
As for its apocalyptic nature...

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.300
You'll have to see for yourselves 
on the day of the game!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:15.310
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.560
<i>Thus, three days later,</i>

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.560
<b>3 Days Later</b>

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.810
<i>at 8:00 in the evening,</i>

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.820
<i>in the looming skyscraper 
known as the Starside Hotel...</i>

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:30.700
<i>Tonight, these people in hefty debt to 
Teiai will experience pandemonium itself.</i>

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:34.710
<i>Enticed ruthlessly, and without mercy, 
into a party from the darkest pits of hell!</i>

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:40.580
<i>The most diabolical of all gambles, 
the Human Derby, is beginning!</i>

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.730
<i>And despite themselves, they are 
filled with anticipation and chills!</i>

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.100
<i>And yet...</i>

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.050
<i>Its contents are so viciously malicious,</i>

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:54.600
<i>so extremely inhumane that, much to our 
chagrin, we can't show them to you!</i>

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.460
<i>So we will be skipping it!</i>

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.890
<i>We can't show it to you! 
But of course we want to!</i>

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.050
<i>We want you to see the gory details!</i>

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:05.880
<u>Please wait a moment!</u>

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:06.860
<i>But!</i>

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:11.050
<i>Nope! Thanks to our overwhelming 
compliance with broadcast standards,</i>

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:18.620
<b>Nope... Nope... Nope...</b>

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.340
<i>We! Cannot! Show you!</i>

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:22.290
<i>As a means of consolation, you can 
seek out this night that one man...</i>

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.960
<i>One legendary man who lived through 
the events of a night like this!</i>

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.970
<i>Yes! In order to witness the full 
scope of this diabolical diversion,</i>

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.220
<i>you must await the arrival of Itou Kaiji!</i>

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.630
<i>Yamazaki had arranged for 
time off on this day.</i>

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.980
<i>He had personal business to attend to, 
and put in for it a week in advance.</i>

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.480
<i>The Human Derby is probably 
starting right about now.</i>

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:51.990
<i>But regarding what he spent 
it doing... we can't show you!</i>

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.540
<i>We'll be skipping it! Not out 
of any sort of compliance,</i>

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:58.740
<i>but because it is so painfully ordinary, 
we're skipping the details!</i>

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.000
<b>Juujuu Barbecue</b>

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.750
You're terrible,

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:08.500
cramming so much meat onto 
the grill at once like this!

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:09.840
B-But...

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.600
I mean, we hardly ever get 
yakiniku in the underground!

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.090
The thought of being able 
to eat beef just made me...

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.600
I understand, believe me. 
It happens to me sometimes.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.600
The whispers of your inner 
demons, hungry for flesh...

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.470
Never mind, personal thing.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:31.240
But this way, your next piece will 
burn while you're eating that one!

00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:36.240
<i>I probably should've been 
there, for future reference...</i>

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.370
<i>But it is what it is.</i>

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.780
<i>It's not my fault they fell on the same date.</i>

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:47.810
<i>Though, with a name like "Human Derby,"</i>

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.400
<i>I have a vague idea of 
what's probably going on.</i>

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.520
Run, Human Kazutakaiser!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.020
W-Wait! Human Yukioh!

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:08.020
No! We can't pass him!

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.640
Take your punishment! 
Punishment! Punishment!

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:16.910
<b>Wrong!!</b>

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:16.910
<i>Wrong!</i>

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.830
<i>The truth is far more diabolical 
than what Yamazaki is imagining!</i>

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:24.180
Go on, get a move on!

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.030
Wh-What the hell is this?!

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.260
Get in there, quick!

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:30.370
Get into the room that 
matches your number, now!

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:33.540
<i>Which is why we can't show you!</i>

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.440
Stop!

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.550
<i>No matter what, embarrassed 
as we might be about it,</i>

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:42.430
Push him! Push him! Push him!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.450
<i>we are forced to omit this part!</i>

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.690
<i>Dan Quixote!</i>

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.350
<b>Try Me (^^)h</b>

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.550
What is this?

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.710
A shock pen?

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:54.780
Oh, yeah, they give you 
that little electric zap...

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.170
Seriously?

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.500
<i>That zap was way too strong!</i>

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.420
<i>Well, not that it'd be fatal or anything...</i>

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.560
Th-The wind!

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.750
<i>Nope, we can't show you!</i>

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:21.560
<i>But look at this face!</i>

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:29.810
<i>We want you to imagine what 
is happening right now!</i>

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:40.820
<i>Okay...</i>

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:45.040
<i>I can do this. I can make it there.</i>

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.580
<i>Yamazaki makes his occasional 
stop at the climbing wall.</i>

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.930
<i>Okay... in one good spurt.</i>

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:54.210
<i>Thus, he does not know...</i>

00:10:55.910 --> 00:11:00.180
<i>that right now, at the Starside Hotel...</i>

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.010
<i>hell is unfolding!</i>

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.640
I guess I'm not there yet.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.780
<b>Line</b>

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.780
Twenty unread posts?

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:18.590
<i>Psst...</i>

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:23.780
<i>It was Team Tonegawa's group chat 
(excluding Tonegawa himself).</i>

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:26.640
<i>Bad... this is bad!</i>

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:29.170
<i>This is what they meant by "Human Derby"?</i>

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.390
<i>This is too crazy...</i>

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:33.790
<i>Calling this "The Brave Men Road" 
is way too innocent-sounding...</i>

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.580
<i>Stars...</i>

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.800
<i>You're right, stars... 
just like the name implies.</i>

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.240
<i>There's no wind blowing, though.</i>

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:40.710
<i>This is too hardcore! Hard! Core!</i>

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:42.010
<i>Electricity...</i>

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.300
<i>They keep saying it's crazy... 
Is it really that bad?</i>

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:49.310
<b>What's up?</b>

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.310
<b>Read</b>

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.310
<i>It's been read...</i>

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:53.810
<i>Then... "What was the Human Derby like"?</i>

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.830
<i>Yamazaki-san...
The Human Derby was basically...</i>

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:01.880
<i>Basically...?</i>

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.690
<i>Out of juice?</i>

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.830
<i>That was a close one! Too close!</i>

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.470
<i>Out of battery!</i>

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:12.080
Oh, well. I can ask tomorrow.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.580
<i>Unfortunately, in the end...</i>

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.840
<i>We just can't show you! No matter what!</i>

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.520
<i>Money is more valuable than life.</i>

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.460
The Middle Management Blues of...

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.020
Tonegawa-sense—

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:39.560
<i>On this day, one of Team Tonegawa's 
members, Ogino Keiichi...</i>

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.280
<i>is getting married!</i>

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.530
<b>Ogino Family
Ishida Family
Wedding Ceremony</b>

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.420
<i>A major milestone in life, 
with a major celebration to match!</i>

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:49.530
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.360
Nakata! Damn it, what are you doing?!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.040
That violates etiquette!

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:57.670
<i>Wearing sunglasses to a wedding, 
of course, is a breach of etiquette.</i>

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:01.800
That's out! Teiai employee or not, 
no black neckties!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.810
Really?!

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.550
Congratulations.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.680
Thank you.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:15.170
<i>At Teiai, there's a silent rule observed 
for gifts at ceremonies like these:</i>

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.890
<i>Coworkers give 30,000 yen!</i>

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.070
<i>Superiors give 50,000!</i>

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.150
<i>Hard cash only!</i>

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.950
<i>These are Teiai's rules for mature gift-giving!</i>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.360
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:35.460
Oh, it's Kikuchi, Nagata, and Ogino!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.720
No, sir! That's the groom!

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.330
I know. You're Hagio.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:42.960
Right!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.120
It's been a while, sir.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.370
Ogino invited us.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.970
I see you've all adapted to the 
South Hateruma Island office.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:54.930
You think so?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.850
It's all over your faces.

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.610
Not just our faces, sir!

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.150
The coral reef snakes got us!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.280
Cover those up. Let's get in there.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.090
Uh, Tonegawa-sensei...

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:22.130
Who's that guy sitting across from us?

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.010
Why would he be at the same table?

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:30.270
Oh, most likely a friend who doesn't 
have any mutual friends with the couple.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.450
Happens all the time.

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.860
I-I see...

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:35.020
Ladies and gentlemen, it's time to begin.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.520
Here are the bride and groom!

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:42.490
If you could all give them 
a warm round of applause!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.130
<i>For what is likely the only time 
in his life, a Teiai man in black</i>

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:51.740
<i>becomes a man in white.</i>

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.740
The bride is so pretty!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:59.860
Now, we'll have a few words 
from the groom's boss,

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:05.500
Tonegawa Yukio-sama from the Teiai 
Corporation, who's here to congratulate them.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:08.490
My name is Tonegawa.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:13.780
It's a pleasure to be here 
on such a joyous occasion.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:19.570
If I could describe the groom in one word, 
it'd be "quiet." He doesn't talk much,

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.520
but he always gets his work done. 
He is a very talented individual.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:29.410
Although at times, he's so quiet that I have 
trouble telling if he's actually around...

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:34.230
<i>The speech is neither too long nor too short,</i>

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:37.130
<i>punctuated by bits of humor to 
keep the atmosphere upbeat.</i>

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.980
<i>Excellent work, Tonegawa!</i>

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:43.140
This will be their first job 
together as a married couple!

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:44.950
<i>Time to cut the cake!</i>

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:48.050
<i>The event is recorded for posterity!</i>

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.800
<i>And then, the banquet begins.</i>

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.800
You surprised me, sir.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:58.280
I didn't know you thought so highly of Ogino.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:02.690
I bet he was really happy to hear all that.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.260
Fool.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:10.650
None of that speech was true.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.590
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:18.120
Those kinds of congratulatory speeches 
are, in essence, about setting a tone.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:24.120
They just want to relax. They don't 
care about the truth of the matter,

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:28.480
so you just tell them the bride 
and groom are wonderful people.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.130
I see...

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.260
If we could interrupt for a moment...

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:38.770
While the bride and groom are getting 
changed, we have on the big screen

00:16:38.770 --> 00:16:43.020
a special movie to show us 
the highlights of their lives!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.520
That sounds like fun!

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.500
<i>Fairly typical course of events...</i>

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:52.940
<i>I've attended more weddings 
than I can remember,</i>

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:55.330
<i>so I've grown bored with this custom.</i>

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.650
Thirty-five years ago,

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:04.040
the groom, Ogino Keiichi-san, was born in 
the Republic of Zambia, in southern Africa.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:06.290
Zambia?!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.350
I had no idea! Ogino-san was born overseas?

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:13.770
Yeah, he told me about it once!

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:16.970
He returned to Japan at the age 
of eight, and after coming of age,

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.700
he tried several different careers.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:22.060
At the age of 25, he even tried 
his hand at the world of comedy.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.450
Comedy?!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:25.890
Tonegawa-sensei, that's...

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:31.570
Keiichi-san formed a duo called 
Volt Amperes, taking to the stage.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:35.290
<i>H-His old partner?!</i>

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.850
<i>Not an uncommon occurrence:</i>

00:17:36.850 --> 00:17:39.820
<i>learning surprising things about 
the groom at his wedding!</i>

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.380
<i>The food's a bit above average.</i>

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.920
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.730
How'd it go, Saemon?

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:54.060
Yes, sir. I checked with Tsukui, 
the master of ceremonies,

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:58.360
and neither the bride nor the groom's 
side have anything strange planned.

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.180
I see.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.930
Ogino has has some sense.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.950
To drag people out on a Sunday,

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:09.690
expecting them to pay thirty or fifty 
thousand yen, and then make them watch

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.340
a bunch of terrible limbo dancing 
that nobody wants to see,

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.190
or amateur-level self-absorbed karaoke...

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:18.950
It would be like hell on Earth! 
Some sort of penalty!

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:21.350
I-I see.

00:18:21.350 --> 00:18:23.200
<i>Just as Saemon-Saburou said...</i>

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:27.820
And now, we have some congratulatory 
letters for the newlyweds.

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:31.630
First is a message celebrating their union 
from the president of the Teiai Group,

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:33.880
<i>After that, no particularly awkward 
diversions or speeches are performed,</i>

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:34.900
Hyoudou Kazutaka-sama...

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:36.970
<i>and the reception continues 
without incident.</i>

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:41.380
<i>After they address the crowd,</i>

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>there'll probably just be some 
pictures taken, and it'll be over.</i>

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.370
<b>Aim for 100,000 Followers</b>

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.230
<i>Meanwhile, on a basement level at Teiai...</i>

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:49.980
Congratu

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.940
<i>Congratulations, Ogino-san!</i>

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.990
<i>Ebitani posts a congratulatory tweet.</i>

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:58.740
Excuse me!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.240
Can we get some more natural-looking smiles?

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.080
<i>Yamazaki handles the photography.</i>

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.630
Okay, that looks good!

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:10.120
All right, three... two... one!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:16.000
Start the music!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:22.260
<i>What is this music that sounds 
like something off a gym mix?</i>

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:36.710
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.280
<i>A flash mob?!</i>

00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:42.410
What is it?

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:44.030
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.050
What the heck?

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:51.040
<i>Those idiots! And after I warned them about 
this kind of half-baked entertainment!</i>

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:06.330
The groom, too?! Yeah!

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:15.080
<i>I see...</i>

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:20.570
<i>As half-baked as it is, it conveys a message.</i>

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:23.070
<i>One of celebration...</i>

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:28.080
<i>In essence, I suppose that's what 
the mood is today, isn't it?</i>

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.040
<i>Good grief...</i>

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.290
<i>I suppose there's no choice.</i>

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.210
<i>I'm in.</i>

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:49.570
<i>An overwhelming celebration!</i>

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:51.770
<i>Congratulations!</i>

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the one known as the 
number-two man in the Teiai Group.</i>

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:01.820
<i>This is the story of his struggles 
between his employer, the president,</i>

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.580
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:10.970
<i>The story of one man... and the 
good times he sometimes shares.</i>

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.040
<i>Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.120
<i>Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:50.050 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Thank you for watching.</b>

00:22:50.050 --> 00:23:00.250
Illustration by: Takada Haruhito
